# LINE ENDINGS, AND WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so a fresh clone gets CRLF in
# the working tree. That broke 27 tests with "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected
# token" and no useful location, and it took a while to find: vitest transforms
# a module by hoisting its imports to the top, and tools/inspect-model.mjs and
# tools/declare.mjs both start with a `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang. Hoisting
# pushes the shebang to line 3, where it is a syntax error rather than a shebang.
#
# It surfaced here the moment a `git checkout` re-wrote those two files with
# CRLF. On a machine that had never seen them any other way it would have been
# the FIRST thing a new clone did, which is a poor welcome for a repo that has
# just been published.
#
# So: LF in the working tree, everywhere, on every platform. The tools are run
# by node, python and pwsh, all of which are happy with LF on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries a line-ending or diff conversion on them.
*.glb    binary
*.png    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.stp    binary
*.step   binary
